{"name":"Postmodern Mauve","hex":"#b39c8e","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"postmodern","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Relating to what follows the modern era. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","Of, relating to, or having the characteristics of postmodernism, especially as represented in art, architecture, literature, science, or philosophy that reacts against an earlier modernism."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A postmodernist."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/postmodern"},{"term":"mauve","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A rich purple synthetic dye, which faded easily, briefly popular c. 1859‒1873 and now called mauveine.","A pale purple or violet colour, like the colour of the dye after it has faded."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a pale purple colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mauve"}],"entries":[{"title":"Postmodernism","blocks":[{"text":"Postmodernism encompasses a variety of artistic, cultural, and philosophical movements. It emerged in the mid-20th century as a skeptical response to modernism, emphasizing the instability of meaning, rejection of universal truths, and critique of grand narratives. While its definition varies across disciplines, it commonly involves skepticism toward established norms, blending of styles, and attention to the socially constructed nature of knowledge and reality."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/London_-_Vauxhall_Bridge_Road_-_South_Bank_-_Jubilee_Walkway_-_View_East_on_SIS_%28MI6_-_Secret_Intelligence_Services%29_Building_1989-94_by_Terry_Farrell.jpg/330px-London_-_Vauxhall_Bridge_Road_-_South_Bank_-_Jubilee_Walkway_-_View_East_on_SIS_%28MI6_-_Secret_Intelligence_Services%29_Building_1989-94_by_Terry_Farrell.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Postmodernism"},{"title":"Mauve","blocks":[{"text":"Mauve is a pale purple color named after the mallow flower. The first use of the word mauve as a color was in 1796–1798 according to the Oxford English Dictionary, but its use seems to have been rare before 1859. Another name for the color is mallow, with the first recorded use of mallow as a color name in English in 1611."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/Wilde_Malve.JPG/330px-Wilde_Malve.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mauve"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/Creeley.jpg/500px-Creeley.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/Creeley.jpg/500px-Creeley.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The poet Robert Creeley in 1972","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACreeley.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/9/95/Warhol-Campbell_Soup-1-screenprint-1968.jpg/250px-Warhol-Campbell_Soup-1-screenprint-1968.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/95/Warhol-Campbell_Soup-1-screenprint-1968.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/9/95/Warhol-Campbell_Soup-1-screenprint-1968.jpg/250px-Warhol-Campbell_Soup-1-screenprint-1968.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Andy Warhol's Campbell's Soup I (1968)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWarhol-Campbell_Soup-1-screenprint-1968.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Portland_Building_1982.jpg/500px-Portland_Building_1982.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org